LazInk licensing
================

MIT, for every file in the package. See LICENSES/MIT.txt.

Until 18 September 2026 this said something longer: the renderer was derived
from Project JEDI's JVCL and stayed under MPL 1.1, so the package carried two
licenses and anyone shipping a program built with it owed recipients that
renderer's source. That renderer is gone. LazInk draws with its own engine
now - inkrender.pas, inkbox.pas and inkdraw.pas - and no third-party code
remains in the package. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for the history and the
credit, which stand whatever the license says.

Lazarus/LCL and Free Pascal are dependencies with their own licenses; they
are not relicensed by LazInk.

The intended destination is a license with no conditions at all - 0BSD, as
ROADMAP.md section 4 sets out. One thing stands between here and there:
inklistbox.pas grew out of wp's forum list box example, and what remains of
that example has to be confirmed or rewritten before the package can be
relicensed again. MIT until then.

